    {
      "title": "Dozens reported injured in Yemeni Houthi attack at Riyadh airport",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/10/yemen-government-allied-forces-recapture-bab-al-mandab-strait-houthis-taiz",
      "description": "<p>Saudi authorities yet to confirm strike as government-allied forces in Yemen claim successful offensive to retake Bab al-Mandab strait</p><p>Yemen’s Houthis have launched a missile attack on Riyadh’s international airport in Saudi Arabia, with dozens reported wounded and a witness describing panic in the terminal.</p><p>Saudi authorities did not confirm any new attack or evacuation, but one witness reported hearing an explosion while waiting to board a flight, and another said they saw a strike that left people wounded.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/10/yemen-government-allied-forces-recapture-bab-al-mandab-strait-houthis-taiz\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-10T15:54:12"
    },
    {
      "title": "Riyadh Airport Attacked Again, Diplomats Say, After Days of Houthi Strikes",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/10/world/middleeast/riyadh-airport-attack-energy-congress.html",
      "description": "Flights were diverted from the airport in the capital of Saudi Arabia, which has faced repeated deadly attacks from the Iran-backed militia in Yemen.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-10T16:14:19"
    },
    {
      "title": "Riyadh airport evacuated after reported fresh attack, say officials",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/riyadh-airport-evacuated-after-reported-fresh-attack-say-officials-126101000780_1.html",
      "description": "Two regional officials say the airport in the Saudi capital has been attacked again.\nOne official said the Riyadh airport has been evacuated, and the other said air traffic has stopped. They spoke on condition of anonymity because they weren't authorised to speak to the media.\nKing Khalid International Airport has been targeted multiple times this week, with three Saudi civilians including a pilot killed on Thursday.\nIran-backed Houthi rebels in neighbouring Yemen have claimed responsibility for those attacks. There was no immediate Houthi statement Saturday.\nThe airport issued a terse alert telling passengers to check with airlines to confirm flights before going there.\nFighting in Yemen between the Houthis and the Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces has escalated, with a Saudi-led coalition providing air support for government forces in an attempt to reverse recent Houthi gains along the Red Sea.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T14:37:26"
    }
